## R-transparency proof, check 4: one Opacity 0.4 blocker between the
## receiver and light -- reads between transparencyshadow_none.rib (no
## blocker) and transparencyshadow_opaque.rib (opaque blocker). The
## blocker is a closed sphere, so the shadow ray crosses its near and far
## shell alike: transmission is (1 - Os)^2, one factor per surface
## crossed, not per blocker. Not third-party.
Display "transparencyshadow_one.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 320 240 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [45]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.04]
LightSource "distantlight" 2 "intensity" [1.45] "lightcolor" [1 1 1]
	"from" [5 2 -3] "to" [0 0 0]
Sides 1
Surface "matte" "Ka" [0.2] "Kd" [0.8]

AttributeBegin
	Translate 0 0 7
	Sphere 3 -3 3 360
AttributeEnd

AttributeBegin
	Translate 1.8 0.8 3.5
	Opacity [0.4 0.4 0.4]
	Sphere 0.6 -0.6 0.6 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
